  "external_evidence": [
    "missing_row_*: the store keeps no record of whether the key was deleted. If the last committed operation on the key was a write, the row is lost; if it was a delete, the entry is a dangling index entry vacuum left behind (autovacuum does not sweep index entries). Settle each key against: a standby (it applies logical frames, so it holds the row if it was not deleted); the logical transaction log, or the commit-log archive, for the key's last operation; archived page-log segments, rolled forward into a scratch copy up to before the page's re-allocation, which expose the row's bytes; or a backup taken after the last write. In a database, a live secondary-index entry or foreign key that still names the record also proves the row was not deleted."
